error[V0206]: `?` works on a `Result`, and this is `Option<i32>`; `load` returns `Result<i32, string>`
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0206_option_in_result_function/main.vr:9:17
  |
9 |     let value = find(id)?;
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^ `?` works on a `Result`, and this is `Option<i32>`; `load` returns `Result<i32, string>`
  |
  = note: `?` on an `Option` needs a function that returns an `Option`; use `match` to look inside it
  = note: in Rust terms, `?` returns early with the `Err` or the `None`, so the function's return type must be a `Result` with the same error type, or an `Option`
